[{"source" ":org/Math-Academy" "forms" [[:db/retract 17592186230997 :answer-field/choices 17592186230998] [:db/retract 17592186230997 :answer-field/choices 17592186230999] [:db/retract 17592186230997 :answer-field/choices 17592186231000] [:db/retract 17592186230997 :answer-field/choices 17592186231001] [:db/retract 17592186230997 :answer-field/choices 17592186231002] {:db/id 17592186231450 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-70f30638-2aaa-5352-bc26-9df3570b67f9" "question-bcdc2275-c8f5-5708-9f40-dd5af1bab702" "question-dae35b84-ab79-5551-9374-7336192ddee8" "question-c1599c17-000c-53e6-a6c2-601e2c06fa87"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186231376 :question/problem "Let $S=\\{-1,0,2,4\\}$ and suppose\n\n$$\nf(-1)=3,\\qquad f(0)=-2,\\qquad f(2)=5,\\qquad f(4)=1.\n$$\n\nCompute the following:\n\n$$\n\\max_{x \\in S} f(x),\\qquad \\arg\\max_{x \\in S} f(x),\\qquad \\min_{x \\in S} f(x),\\qquad \\arg\\min_{x \\in S} f(x).\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that \n\n- $\\max\\limits_{x \\in S} f(x)$ is the largest output value, while\n\n- $\\arg\\max\\limits_{x \\in S} f(x)$ is an input in $S$ where that largest output occurs.\n\nOn the other hand,\n\n- $\\min\\limits_{x \\in S} f(x)$ is the smallest output value, while\n\n- $\\arg\\min\\limits_{x \\in S} f(x)$ is an input in $S$ where that smallest output occurs.\n\nThe outputs of $f$ on $S$ are\n\n$$\n3,\\qquad -2,\\qquad 5,\\qquad 1.\n$$\n\nThe largest output is $5,$ and it occurs at $x=2.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\max_{x \\in S} f(x)=5,\n\\qquad\n\\arg\\max_{x \\in S} f(x)=2.\n$$\n\nSimilarly, the smallest output is $-2,$ and it occurs at $x=0.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\min_{x \\in S} f(x)=-2,\n\\qquad\n\\arg\\min_{x \\in S} f(x)=0.\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186231451 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-d67215f0-5168-5f34-aa11-965cede50421" "question-c31456f2-6f7b-5c43-b2d6-d63a185e088a" "question-6b85f086-3ff0-5996-862a-13fba81da102" "question-53479689-99f5-53fc-9bbf-170474b20c8c"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186231377 :question/problem "Let $S=\\{-1,0,2,3\\}$ and suppose\n\n$$\nf(-1)=4,\\qquad f(0)=1,\\qquad f(2)=4,\\qquad f(3)=2.\n$$\n\nCompute $\\max_{x \\in S} f(x)$ and $\\arg\\max_{x \\in S} f(x).$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that \n\n- $\\max\\limits_{x \\in S} f(x)$ is the largest output value, while\n\n- $\\arg\\max\\limits_{x \\in S} f(x)$ is an input in $S$ where that largest output occurs.\n\nThe output values are $4,1,4,$ and $2.$ The maximum output value is $4.$\n\nThis maximum occurs at both $x=-1$ and $x=2.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\max_{x \\in S} f(x)=\\bbox[4pt,border: 1px solid lightgray]{4}\n\\qquad \\textrm{and} \\qquad\n\\arg\\max_{x \\in S} f(x)=\\bbox[4pt,border: 1px solid lightgray]{\\{-1,2\\}}.\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186231452 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-b99f27b6-bb0f-5afc-b357-d0b316cf7a24" "question-f7168caf-99d8-56ba-8b1b-f286cb0133ec" "question-00fdbc42-937e-5a35-be79-3ffa566504b0" "question-f072186e-d0b3-5257-aa50-624c55328198" "question-0e94aa36-f8ac-5d68-8a85-88c135136bde"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186231378 :question/problem "Let $S$ be a set and let $f$ be a real-valued function on $S.$ Consider the expression\n\n$$\nx^*=\\arg\\max_{x \\in S} f(x).\n$$\n\nWhat does this statement mean in words? Also, what does $\\max_{x \\in S} f(x)$ represent?" :question/worked-solution "The expression $x^*=\\arg\\max_{x \\in S} f(x)$ means that:\n\n- $x^*$ is an input value in $S.$\n\n- Among all $x \\in S,$ the value $f(x^*)$ is as large as possible.\n\nIn other words, $x^*$ is a choice of input where $f$ attains its largest value on $S.$\n\nBy contrast, $\\max_{x \\in S} f(x)$ is not an input. It is the largest *function value* that $f$ attains on $S.$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "question-70f30638-2aaa-5352-bc26-9df3570b67f9" :question/id #uuid "70f30638-2aaa-5352-bc26-9df3570b67f9" :question/math-academy-id "q-355268" :question/problem "Let $S=\\{-2,0,1,4\\}$ and suppose\n\n$$\nh(-2)=3,\\,h(0)=7,\\,h(1)=-5,\\,h(4)=2.\n$$\n\nCompute the following:\n\n${max}_{x\\in S}h(x)=$\n{{field-1}}\n\n$\\operatorname{arg}⁡{max}_{x\\in S}h(x)=$\n{{field-2}}\n\n${min}_{x\\in S}h(x)=$\n{{field-3}}\n\n$\\operatorname{arg}⁡{min}_{x\\in S}h(x)=$\n{{field-4}}" :question/worked-solution "Recall that \n\n- ${max}_{x\\in S}h(x)$ is the largest output value, while\n\n- $\\operatorname{arg}⁡{max}_{x\\in S}h(x)$ is an input in $S$ where that largest output occurs.\n\nOn the other hand,\n\n- ${min}_{x\\in S}h(x)$ is the smallest output value, while\n\n- $\\operatorname{arg}⁡{min}_{x\\in S}h(x)$ is an input in $S$ where that smallest output occurs.\n\nHere, the outputs are $3,7,-5,$ and $2.$ \n\n- The largest output is $7,$ and it occurs at $x=0.$\n\n- The smallest output is $-5,$ and it occurs at $x=1.$\n\nTherefore, we have the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{max}_{x\\in S}h(x) & =7 \\\\ \\operatorname{arg}⁡{max}_{x\\in S}h(x) & =0 \\\\ {min}_{x\\in S}h(x) & =-5 \\\\ \\operatorname{arg}⁡{min}_{x\\in S}h(x) & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-1ee30075-ef1d-5646-bf59-1a1cf206b83f" "answer-field-45974829-4fca-57ca-9073-a7dd2f9bde6c" "answer-field-081ebd9b-ca0f-5b1c-89d9-c6f0062cfe66" "answer-field-7eb194c3-5312-5415-a2f8-09fa9542b93e"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-1ee30075-ef1d-5646-bf59-1a1cf206b83f" :answer-field/id #uuid "1ee30075-ef1d-5646-bf59-1a1cf206b83f" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-44861867-4f69-5756-847f-d2aa71df7223" :answer-field/choices ["answer-44861867-4f69-5756-847f-d2aa71df7223"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-44861867-4f69-5756-847f-d2aa71df7223" :answer/id #uuid "44861867-4f69-5756-847f-d2aa71df7223" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "7" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/i