uuid "b99f27b6-bb0f-5afc-b357-d0b316cf7a24" :question/math-academy-id "q-355392" :question/problem "Which of the following best describes $\\operatorname{arg}⁡{max}_{\\theta \\in [0,2\\pi ]}f(\\theta )?$" :question/worked-solution "By definition, $\\operatorname{arg}⁡max$ returns an input value where the function achieves its maximum value. \n\nTherefore, $\\operatorname{arg}⁡{max}_{\\theta \\in [0,2\\pi ]}f(\\theta )$ is the value of $\\theta $ in $[0,2\\pi ]$ where $f(\\theta )$ is largest." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-0834d9ef-3a48-5a32-a4fd-6b4392e97da5"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-0834d9ef-3a48-5a32-a4fd-6b4392e97da5" :answer-field/id #uuid "0834d9ef-3a48-5a32-a4fd-6b4392e97da5" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-f76c7c1f-2951-5978-a2f9-0a0b65916cfd" :answer-field/choices ["answer-97bf954f-753a-55e5-a496-69bf543f8ca2" "answer-36b15808-5d17-588e-96b0-4bafa73d3a87" "answer-03cc3ad8-5803-5027-8ae1-b9ab3dc36bf0" "answer-f76c7c1f-2951-5978-a2f9-0a0b65916cfd" "answer-109bb7e4-12e9-5e6e-a2c9-4a3ea3215fc9"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-97bf954f-753a-55e5-a496-69bf543f8ca2" :answer/id #uuid "97bf954f-753a-55e5-a496-69bf543f8ca2" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "The average value of $f(\\theta )$ on $[0,2\\pi ].$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-36b15808-5d17-588e-96b0-4bafa73d3a87" :answer/id #uuid "36b15808-5d17-588e-96b0-4bafa73d3a87" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "The largest value of $f(\\theta )$ on $[0,2\\pi ].$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-03cc3ad8-5803-5027-8ae1-b9ab3dc36bf0" :answer/id #uuid "03cc3ad8-5803-5027-8ae1-b9ab3dc36bf0" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "The smallest value of $f(\\theta )$ on $[0,2\\pi ].$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f76c7c1f-2951-5978-a2f9-0a0b65916cfd" :answer/id #uuid "f76c7c1f-2951-5978-a2f9-0a0b65916cfd" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "The value of $\\theta $ in $[0,2\\pi ]$ where $f(\\theta )$ is largest." :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-109bb7e4-12e9-5e6e-a2c9-4a3ea3215fc9" :answer/id #uuid "109bb7e4-12e9-5e6e-a2c9-4a3ea3215fc9" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "The value of $\\theta $ in $[0,2\\pi ]$ where $f(\\theta )$ is smallest." :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-f7168caf-99d8-56ba-8b1b-f286cb0133ec" :question/id #uuid "f7168caf-99d8-56ba-8b1b-f286cb0133ec" :question/math-academy-id "q-355394" :question/problem "Let $g(y)$ be a profit for product $y,$ where $y\\in \\{3,7,11,15\\}.$ We want to write the best product $\\overset{^}{y}$ as \"the value of $y$ that makes $g(y)$ as large as possible.\"\n\nWhich of the following correctly defines $\\overset{^}{y}?$" :question/worked-solution "We want $\\overset{^}{y}$ to be an *input value* $y$ where the profit $g(y)$ is as large as possible. \n\nThat is exactly what $\\operatorname{arg}⁡max$ returns.\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\overset{^}{y}=\\operatorname{arg}⁡{max}_{y\\in \\{3,7,11,15\\}}g(y).\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-bba509ec-a193-5a29-9ee6-8dfb74ce1d8f"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-bba509ec-a193-5a29-9ee6-8dfb74ce1d8f" :answer-field/id #uuid "bba509ec-a193-5a29-9ee6-8dfb74ce1d8f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-cd1c8e6c-c2cc-567c-b331-4c30a5590e84" :answer-field/choices ["answer-cd1c8e6c-c2cc-567c-b331-4c30a5590e84" "answer-aefadc2d-31ef-5613-926b-0f541f57d23f" "answer-4e419701-4ca0-5634-aac0-e3a2e78a3ba0" "answer-3613e1aa-20ff-553e-86bf-6acd4c4e754b" "answer-70459e85-62ef-5e1c-8027-39db3fe41145"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-cd1c8e6c-c2cc-567c-b331-4c30a5590e84" :answer/id #uuid "cd1c8e6c-c2cc-567c-b331-4c30a5590e84" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\overset{^}{y}=\\operatorname{arg}⁡{max}_{y\\in \\{3,7,11,15\\}}g(y)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-aefadc2d-31ef-5613-926b-0f541f57d23f" :answer/id #uuid "aefadc2d-31ef-5613-926b-0f541f57d23f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\overset{^}{y}=\\operatorname{arg}⁡{min}_{y\\in \\{3,7,11,15\\}}g(y)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-4e419701-4ca0-5634-aac0-e3a2e78a3ba0" :answer/id #uuid "4e419701-4ca0-5634-aac0-e3a2e78a3ba0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\overset{^}{y}=\\operatorname{arg}⁡{min}_{y\\in g(y)}\\{3,7,11,15\\}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-3613e1aa-20ff-553e-86bf-6acd4c4e754b" :answer/id #uuid "3613e1aa-20ff-553e-86bf-6acd4c4e754b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\overset{^}{y}={max}_{y\\in \\{3,7,11,15\\}}g(y)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-70459e85-62ef-5e1c-8027-39db3fe41145" :answer/id #uuid "70459e85-62ef-5e1c-8027-39db3fe41145" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\overset{^}{y}={min}_{y\\in \\{3,7,11,15\\}}g(y)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-00fdbc42-937e-5a35-be79-3ffa566504b0" :question/id #uuid "00fdbc42-937e-5a35-be79-3ffa566504b0" :question/math-academy-id "q-355398" :question/problem "Let $c(n)$ be a cost for option $n,$ where $n\\in \\{3,5,7,9\\}.$ We want to write the optimal option $\\overset{^}{n}$ as \"the value of $n$ that makes $c(n)$ as small as possible.\"\n\nWhich of the following correctly defines $\\overset{^}{n}?$" :question/worked-solution "We want $\\overset{^}{n}$ to be an *input value* $n$ where the cost $c(n)$ is as small as possible. \n\nThat is exactly what $\\operatorname{arg}⁡min$ returns.\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\overset{^}{n}=\\operatorname{arg}⁡{min}_{n\\in \\{3,5,7,9\\}}c(n).\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-fe7e58b2-6cf5-5dc0-a908-c4dfec9a9926"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-fe7e58b2-6cf5-5dc0-a908-c4dfec9a9926" :answer-field/id #uuid "fe7e58b2-6cf5-5dc0-a908-c4dfec9a9926" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-7ed4b9d4-3874-51d6-9f79-7bcc2fe66aae" :answer-field/choices ["answer-6cf15706-6c17-5503-a77a-8bf5a0786d70" "answer-711ef5c5-455c-5d83-901c-33b80c3e7152" "answer-7ed4b9d4-3874-51d6-9f79-7bcc2fe66aae" "answer-0cdf484b-66eb-5a9f-96fb-2be6f97d6737" "answer-1ebe1402-cc23-504b-bb1f-600375c70556"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-6cf15706-6c17-5503-a77a-8bf5a0786d70" :answer/id #uuid "6cf15706-6c17-5503-a77a-8bf5a0786d70" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\overset{^}{n}=\\operatorname{arg}⁡{max}_{n\\in \\{3,5,7,9\\}}c(n)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-711ef5c5-455c-5d83-901c-33b80c3e7152" :answer/id #uuid "711ef5c5-455c-5d83-901c-33b80c3e7152" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\overset{^}{n}=\\operatorname{arg}⁡{max}_{n\\in c(n)}\\{3,5,7,9\\}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-7ed4b9d4-3874-51d6-9f79-7bcc2fe66aae" :answer/id #uuid "7ed4b9d4-3874-51d6-9f79-7bcc2fe66aae" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\overset{^}{n}=\\operatorname{arg}⁡{min}_{n\\in \\{3,5,7,9\\}}c(n)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-0cdf484b-66eb-5a9f-96fb-2be6f97d6737" :answer/id #uuid "0cdf484b-66eb-5a9f-96fb-2be6f97d6737" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\overset{^}{n}={max}_{n\\in \\{3,5,7,9\\}}c(n)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-1ebe1402-cc23-504b-bb1f-600375c70556" :answer/id #uuid "1ebe1402-cc23-504b-bb1f-600375c70556" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\overset{^}{n}={min}_{n\\in \\{3,5,7,9\\}}c(n)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-f072186e-d0b3-5257-aa50-624c55328198" :question/id #uuid "f072186e-d0b3-5257-aa50-624c55328198" :question/math-academy-id "q-355391" :question/problem "Which of the following best describes $\\operatorname{arg}⁡{min}_{x\\in [-1,1]}h(x)?$" :question/worked-solution "By definition, $\\operatorname{arg}⁡min$ returns an input value where the function achieves its minimum value. \n\nTherefore, $\\operatorname{arg}⁡{min}_{x\\in [-1,1]}h(x)$ is the value of $x$ in $[-1,1]$ where $h(x)$ is smallest." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-d2f88345-0eec-5e44-97c9-0e277c06cfc9"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-d2f88345-0eec-5e44-97c9-0e277c06cfc9" :answer-field/id #uuid "d2f88345-0eec-5e44-97c9-0e277c06cfc9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-80db74a6-c35f-567d-a346-735228c01219" :answer-field/choices ["answer-d0ab9aff-a3e4-57ed-9978-6a8fc88bbe0c" "answer-4bae1a6b-5b4f-5d7e-bafc-72b4dd45bce6" "answer-21d18115-9663-5052-9c07-22d8d804669d" "answer-031d6483-a285-51fe-8ffd-764744e050a2" "answer-80db74a6-c35f-567d-a346-735228c01219"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d0ab9aff-a3e4-57ed-9978-6a8fc88bbe0c" :answer/id #uuid "d0ab9aff-a3e4-57ed-9978-6a8fc88bbe0c" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "The average value of $h(x)$ on $[-1,1].$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-4bae1a6b-5b4f-5d7e-bafc-72b4dd45bce6" :answer/id #uuid "4bae1a6b-5b4f-5d7e-bafc-72b4dd45bce6" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "The largest value of $h(x)$ on $[-1,1].$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-21d18115-9663-5052-9c07-22d8d804669d" :answer/id #uuid "21d18115-9663-5052-9c07-22d8d804669d" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "The smallest value of $h(x)$ on $[-1,1].$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-031d6483-a285-51fe-8ffd-764744e050a2" :answer/id #uuid "031d6483-a285-51fe-8ffd-764744e050a2" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "The value of $x$ in $[-1,1]$ where $h(x)$ is largest." :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-80db74a6-c35f-567d-a346-735228c01219" :answer/id #uuid "80db74a6-c35f-567d-a346-735228c01219" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "The value of $x$ in $[-1,1]$ where $h(x)$ is smallest." :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-0e94aa36-f8ac-5d68-8a85-88c135136bde" :question/id #uuid "0e94aa36-f8ac-5d68-8a85-88c135136bde" :question/math-academy-id "q-355401" :question/problem "Let $w(y)$ be a weight for node $y,$ where $y\\in \\{-7,-5,-3,-1\\}.$ We want to write the selected node $\\overset{^}{y}$ as \"the value of $y$ that makes $w(y)$ as large as possible.\"\n\nWhich of the following correctly defines $\\overset{^}{y}?$" :question/worked-solution "We want $\\overset{^}{y}$ to be an *input value* $y$ where the weight $w(y)$ is as large as possible. \n\nThat is exactly what $\\operatorname{arg}⁡max$ returns.\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\overset{^}{y}=\\operatorname{arg}⁡{max}_{y\\in \\{-7,-5,-3,-1\\}}w(y).\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-e07302db-2571-50ff-8138-960f3c5d371d"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-e07302db-2571-50ff-8138-960f3c5d371d" :answer-field/id #uuid "e07302db-2571-50ff-8138-960f3c5d371d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-eed8db63-444d-5be5-abc8-22b87e87b1b0" :answer-field/choices ["answer-eed8db63-444d-5be5-abc8-22b87e87b1b0" "answer-450feb6f-7850-5f5d-8795-282d5fc86d84" "answer-e29d928e-baa8-5e76-b627-c742ea42fee2" "answer-a3f54bd2-c0b3-56c8-b6df-6ffa0ee9341a" "answer-76db008e-9696-50d1-b034-aca1854d279f"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-eed8db63-444d-5be5-abc8-22b87e87b1b0" :answer/id #uuid "eed8db63-444d-5be5-abc8-22b87e87b1b0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\overset{^}{y}=\\operatorname{arg}⁡{max}_{y\\in \\{-7,-5,-3,-1\\}}w(y)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-450feb6f-7850-5f5d-8795-282d5fc86d84" :answer/id #uuid "450feb6f-7850-5f5d-8795-282d5fc86d84" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\overset{^}{y}=\\operatorname{arg}⁡{min}_{y\\in \\{-7,-5,-3,-1\\}}w(y)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e29d928e-baa8-5e76-b627-c742ea42fee2" :answer/id #uuid "e29d928e-baa8-5e76-b627-c742ea42fee2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\overset{^}{y}=\\operatorname{arg}⁡{min}_{y\\in w(y)}\\{-7,-5,-3,-1\\}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a3f54bd2-c0b3-56c8-b6df-6ffa0ee9341a" :answer/id #uuid "a3f54bd2-c0b3-56c8-b6df-6ffa0ee9341a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\overset{^}{y}={max}_{y\\in \\{-7,-5,-3,-1\\}}w(y)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-76db008e-9696-50d1-b034-aca1854d279f" :answer/id #uuid "76db008e-9696-50d1-b034-aca1854d279f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\overset{^}{y}={min}_{y\\in \\{-7,-5,-3,-1\\}}w(y)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186232041 :tutorial/content "In a previous lesson, we used $\\max$ and $\\min$ to talk about the largest and smallest *values* a function can take on a set.\n\nIn this lesson, we learn two closely related pieces of notation:\n\n- $\\max$ and $\\min$ return the best (largest/smallest) *function value*.\n\n- $\\arg\\max$ and $\\arg\\min$ return the *input value* (the \"argument\") where that best value occurs.\n\nFor example, let $S = \\{1,2,3\\}$ and suppose\n\n$$\nf(1)=4,\\qquad f(2)=7,\\qquad f(3)=6.\n$$\n\nThen the largest function value is $7,$ and it occurs when $x=2{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{max}_{x\\in S}f(x) & =7, \\\\ \\operatorname{arg}⁡{max}_{x\\in S}f(x) & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSimilarly, $\\min_{x \\in S} f(x)$ is the smallest function value, and $\\arg\\min_{x \\in S} f(x)$ is an input where that smallest value occurs.\n\n**Watch out!** Sometimes the best value occurs at more than one input. In that case, we need to clarify what $\\arg\\max$ (or $\\arg\\min$) means. We will handle this after we practice the basic case." :db/ensure [:tutorial/validate]} {:db/id 17592186232042 :tutorial/content "Sometimes a function attains its largest (or smallest) value at more than one input. In that case, there are multiple inputs that satisfy the definition of $\\arg\\max$ (or $\\arg\\min$).\n\nIn this course, when a tie occurs, we report the *set* of all inputs where the maximum is achieved as follows:\n\n$$\n\\arg\\max_{x \\in S} f(x) = {x \\in S{:} f(x) = \\max_{u \\in S} f(u)}.\n$$\n\nSimilarly, when a tie occurs, we report the set of all inputs where the minimum is achieved as follows:\n\n$$\n\\arg\\min_{x \\in S} f(x) = {x \\in S{:} f(x) = \\min_{u \\in S} f(u)}.\n$$\n\nThe quantities $\\max_{x \\in S} f(x)$ and $\\min_{x \\in S} f(x)$ are still single numbers." :db/ensure [:tutorial/validate]} {:db/id 17592186231551 :activity/expected-seconds 780.0 :db/ensure [:activity/validate]}] "assertions" [[17592186231376 :question/problem "Let $S=\\{-1,0,2,4\\}$ and suppose\n\n$$\nf(-1)=3,\\qquad f(0)=-2,\\qquad f(2)=5,\\qquad f(4)=1.\n$$\n\nCompute the following:\n\n$$\n\\max_{x \\in S} f(x),\\qquad \\arg\\max_{x \\in S} f(x),\\qquad \\min_{x \\in S} f(x),\\qquad \\arg\\min_{x \\in S} f(x).\n$$"] [17592186231376 :question/worked-solution "Recall that \n\n- $\\max\\limits_{x \\in S} f(x)$ is the largest output value, while\n\n- $\\arg\\max\\limits_{x \\in S} f(x)$ is an input in $S$ where that largest output occurs.\n\nOn the other hand,\n\n- $\\min\\limits_{x \\in S} f(x)$ is the smallest output value, while\n\n- $\\arg\\min\\limits_{x \\in S} f(x)$ is an input in $S$ where that smallest output occurs.\n\nThe outputs of $f$ on $S$ are\n\n$$\n3,\\qquad -2,\\qquad 5,\\qquad 1.\n$$\n\nThe largest output is $5,$ and it occurs at $x=2.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\max_{x \\in S} f(x)=5,\n\\qquad\n\\arg\\max_{x \\in S} f(x)=2.\n$$\n\nSimilarly, the smallest output is $-2,$ and it occurs at $x=0.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\min_{x \\in S} f(x)=-2,\n\\qquad\n\\arg\\min_{x \\in S} f(x)=0.\n$$"] [17592186231377 :question/problem "Let $S=\\{-1,0,2,3\\}$ and suppose\n\n$$\nf(-1)=4,\\qquad f(0)=1,\\qquad f(2)=4,\\qquad f(3)=2.\n$$\n\nCompute $\\max_{x \\in S} f(x)$ and $\\arg\\max_{x \\in S} f(x).$"] [17592186231377 :question/worked-solution "Recall that \n\n- $\\max\\limits_{x \\in S} f(x)$ is the largest output value, while\n\n- $\\arg\\max\\limits_{x \\in S} f(x)$ is an input in $S$ where that largest output occurs.\n\nThe output values are $4,1,4,$ and $2.$ The maximum output value is $4.$\n\nThis maximum occurs at both $x=-1$ and $x=2.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\max_{x \\in S} f(x)=\\bbox[4pt,border: 1px solid lightgray]{4}\n\\qquad \\textrm{and} \\qquad\n\\arg\\max_{x \\in S} f(x)=\\bbox[4pt,border: 1px solid lightgray]{\\{-1,2\\}}.\n$$"] [17592186231378 :question/problem "Let $S$ be a set and let $f$ be a real-valued function on $S.$ Consider the expression\n\n$$\nx^*=\\arg\\max_{x \\in S} f(x).\n$$\n\nWhat does this statement mean in words? Also, what does $\\max_{x \\in S} f(x)$ represent?"] [17592186231378 :question/worked-solution "The expression $x^*=\\arg\\max_{x \\in S} f(x)$ means that:\n\n- $x^*$ is an input value in $S.$\n\n- Among all $x \\in S,$ the value $f(x^*)$ is as large as possible.\n\nIn other words, $x^*$ is a choice of input where $f$ attains its largest value on $S.$\n\nBy contrast, $\\max_{x \\in S} f(x)$ is not an input. It is the largest *function value* that $f$ attains on $S.$"] ["question-70f30638-2aaa-5352-bc26-9df3570b67f9" :question/id #uuid "70f30638-2aaa-5352-bc26-9df3570b67f9"] ["question-70f30638-2aaa-5352-bc26-9df3570b67f9" :question/math-academy-id "q-355268"] ["question-70f30638-2aaa-5352-bc26-9df3570b67f9" :question/problem "Let $S=\\{-2,0,1,4\\}$ and suppose\n\n$$\nh(-2)=3,\\,h(0)=7,\\,h(1)=-5,\\,h(4)=2.\n$$\n\nCompute the following:\n\n${max}_{x\\in S}h(x)=$\n{{field-1}}\n\n$\\operatorname{arg}⁡{max}_{x\\in S}h(x)=$\n{{field-2}}\n\n${min}_{x\\in S}h(x)=$\n{{field-3}}\n\n$\\operatorname{arg}⁡{min}_{x\\in S}h(x)=$\n{{field-4}}"] ["question-70f30638-2aaa-5352-bc26-9df3570b67f9" :question/worked-solution "Recall that \n\n- ${max}_{x\\in S}h(x)$ is the largest output value, while\n\n- $\\operatorname{arg}⁡{max}_{x\\in S}h(x)$ is an input in $S$ where that largest output occurs.\n\nOn the other hand,\n\n- ${min}_{x\\in S}h(x)$ is the smallest output value, while\n\n- $\\operatorname{arg}⁡{min}_{x\\in S}h(x)$ is an input in $S$ where that smallest output occurs.\n\nHere, the outputs are $3,7,-5,$ and $2.$ \n\n- The largest output is $7,$ and it occurs at $x=0.$\n\n- The smallest output is $-5,$ and it occurs at $x=1.$\n\nTherefore, we have the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{max}_{x\\in S}h(x) & =7 \\\\ \\operatorname{arg}⁡{max}_{x\\in S}h(x) & =0 \\\\ {min}_{x\\in S}h(x) & =-5 \\\\ \\operatorname{arg}⁡{min}_{x\\in S}h(x) & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$"] ["question-70f30638-2aaa-5352-bc26-9df3570b67f9" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy] ["answer-field-1ee30075-ef1d-5646-bf59-1a1cf206b83f" :answer-field/id #uuid "1ee30075-ef1d-5646-bf59-1a1cf206b83f"] ["answer-44861867-4f69-5756-847f-d2aa71df7223" :answer/id #uuid "44861867-4f69-5756-847f-d2aa71df7223"] ["answer-44861867-4f69-5756-847f-d2aa71df7223" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-44861867-4f69-5756-847f-d2aa71df7223" :answer/value "7"] ["answer-field-1ee30075-ef1d-5646-bf59-1a1cf206b83f" :answer-field/key "field-1"] ["answer-field-1ee30075-ef1d-5646-bf59-1a1cf206b83f" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank] ["answer-field-1ee30075-ef1d-5646-bf59-1a1cf206b83f" :answer-field/correct "answer-44861867-4f69-5756-847f-d2aa71df7223"] ["answer-field-1ee30075-ef1d-5646-bf59-1a1cf206b83f" :answer-field/choices "answer-44861867-4f69-5756-847f-d2aa71df7223"] ["answer-field-45974829-4fca-57ca-9073-a7dd2f9bde6c" :answer-field/id #uuid "45974829-4fca-57ca-9073-a7dd2f9bde6c"] ["answer-ca040f2a-3108-5cde-a403-58ca2d097882" :answer/id #uuid "ca040f2a-3108-5cde-a403-58ca2d097882"] ["answer-ca040f2a-3108-5cde-a403-58ca2d097882" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-ca040f2a-3108-5cde-a403-58ca2d097882" :answer/value "0"] 